{"id":"08fb6fd463430f87","group":"58","path":"58/batch13/58-df-double-cover.md","title":"Double Cover","display":"df-double-cover — Double Cover","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-double-cover","aliases":["58-df-double-cover","Double Cover"],"display":"df-double-cover — Double Cover","depends_on":["[[../batch19/58-df-covering-space.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-double-cover"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-double-cover</span><span>Double Cover</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-double-cover — Double Cover"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"e93778b32bbd2327\" href=\"?note=e93778b32bbd2327\" title=\"../batch19/58-df-covering-space.md\">../batch19/58-df-covering-space.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"p,\\widetilde X,\\tau_{\\widetilde X},X,\\tau_X\\in V\">\\(p,\\widetilde X,\\tau_{\\widetilde X},X,\\tau_X\\in V\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{CoveringSpace}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{CoveringSpace}_S\\)</span> (covering-space predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"e93778b32bbd2327\" href=\"?note=e93778b32bbd2327\" title=\"../batch19/58-df-covering-space.md\">../batch19/58-df-covering-space.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{DoubleCover}_S\\subseteq V^5\">\\(\\mathrm{DoubleCover}_S\\subseteq V^5\\)</span> (double-cover predicate defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}double\\text{-}cover} \\vdash \\mathrm{DoubleCover}_S(p,\\widetilde X,\\tau_{\\widetilde X},X,\\tau_X)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{CoveringSpace}_S(p,\\widetilde X,\\tau_{\\widetilde X},X,\\tau_X)\\land\\forall x\\in X\\;\\bigl(|p^{-1}[\\{x\\}]|=2\\bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}double\\text{-}cover} \\vdash \\mathrm{DoubleCover}_S(p,\\widetilde X,\\tau_{\\widetilde X},X,\\tau_X)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{CoveringSpace}_S(p,\\widetilde X,\\tau_{\\widetilde X},X,\\tau_X)\\land\\forall x\\in X\\;\\bigl(|p^{-1}[\\{x\\}]|=2\\bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The source and target topologies are explicit and match the five-argument covering-space predicate.</li>\n<li>Double cover: 2-sheeted covering; fundamental group is index 2 subgroup</li>\n<li>Fundamental-group index, quotient by <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"C_2\">\\(C_2\\)</span>, and associated bundle constructions are consequences or applications.</li>\n<li>Under the usual connectedness and local path-connectedness hypotheses, connected double covers correspond to index-<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"2\">\\(2\\)</span> subgroups of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\pi_1(X)\">\\(\\pi_1(X)\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>For a universal cover, the deck group is isomorphic to <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\pi_1(X)\">\\(\\pi_1(X)\\)</span> under the standard semilocally simply connected hypotheses.</li>\n<li>Branched: branched double cover at ramification points; still double cover as varieties</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Reference\">[Reference]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Hatcher, Algebraic Topology</li>\n<li>Fulton, Algebraic Curves</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2},{"id":"Reference","text":"[Reference]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch19/58-df-covering-space.md","status":"resolved","id":"e93778b32bbd2327","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch19/58-df-covering-space.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch19/58-df-covering-space.md","status":"resolved","id":"e93778b32bbd2327","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{CoveringSpace}_S$ (covering-space predicate, see [[../batch19/58-df-covering-space.md]])","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"p,\\widetilde X,\\tau_{\\widetilde X},X,\\tau_X\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{CoveringSpace}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{DoubleCover}_S\\subseteq V^5","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}double\\text{-}cover} \\vdash \\mathrm{DoubleCover}_S(p,\\widetilde X,\\tau_{\\widetilde X},X,\\tau_X)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{CoveringSpace}_S(p,\\widetilde X,\\tau_{\\widetilde X},X,\\tau_X)\\land\\forall x\\in X\\;\\bigl(|p^{-1}[\\{x\\}]|=2\\bigr)","display":true},{"tex":"C_2","display":false},{"tex":"2","display":false},{"tex":"\\pi_1(X)","display":false},{"tex":"\\pi_1(X)","display":false}],"bytes":1537,"backlinks":[{"id":"413736d776e8d283","anchor":"ref-1","locations":["元数据 · depends_on"],"count":1,"excerpt":""},{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-455","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch13/58-df-double-cover.md|58-df-double-cover]]（batch13）"}],"outgoing":["e93778b32bbd2327"]}